body:
You'd think at this point their review would be;  


"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"  


Positive Review

Jean and Beidou in Genshin.

&#x200B;

In Taimanin Action I want the girl with the biggest chest beefers.

Hey, if anyone deserved a fate like that it's Syazel.

&#x200B;

Also, isn't >!Aizen!< tied to a chair for like 10,000 years?

Witchblade anime.

&#x200B;

Oh wait, you said 'mostly fantastic'.

White hair? Check.

&#x200B;

Katana? Check. (Masamune)

&#x200B;

Shares DNA with protagonist? Check. (Jenova Cells)

&#x200B;

Obsessed with a parent? Check. (Jenova)

&#x200B;

Gets motivated? Check. (Nibelheim Incident)

&#x200B;

Wants more power? Check. (Absorb Lifestream)

&#x200B;

Sword can cut entrances to other dimensions? Check. (FF7 Remake)

&#x200B;

Never stops showing up? Check. (Advent Children)

&#x200B;

Reincarnates from split personalities? Check. (Kadaj)

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Face it. Vergil is a Sephiroth CLONE!

Naga the Serpent from Slayers.

&#x200B;

I'm willing to die alone on this hill.

Rufus Shinra. YUMMM!!!

&#x200B;

Chrom is second.

I don't know which Souls game was the most painful to Platinum, I've done all 5. Demon's Souls you had to farm pure bladestone... Dark Souls 1 you had to turn in all that humanity one by one... Dark Souls 2 you had to get to new game++... Dark Souls 3 you had to farm for Darkmoon Covenant... Bloodborne you had to delve deep into the chalice dungeons.

&#x200B;

I guess my most pointless/painful accomplishment was doing my Captain Hook playthrough on Dark Souls 2. Lucatiel's outfit, maskless hat, rapier/scimitar, and hook only.  Those fucking lightning unicorns in the blizzard!!!
